    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0607" n="1341" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1341"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-11-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                    1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Jewett telegraphs massacres have begun at Marsovan and Amasia. Poche telegraphs
                    bloody conflict at Aintab. Great fear is entertained at Aleppo. Anxiety of
                    friends of missionaries might be allayed if the Department of State would
                    authorize public statement that I have not needed Department orders to awaken
                    vigilance, as published, but demanded and secured orders, since renewed and
                    executed, to protect Americans everywhere before any massacres began.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
